+## 2026-09-29 — Fix the GPU bundle's stage-error, C3 and C1 guards and credit its evidence in the notes
+
+Codex verification r1 of the GPU checks receipts merge (`d793d16`, REJECT, `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-merge-gpu-receipts-r1.md`; prompt, transcript and evidence directory committed beside it) found one P2 and four P3s. Code (post-run revisions under `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/gpu-checks-2026-09-29/scripts/`; the as-run `pod/attempt*/` scripts and records are unchanged): `driver.py` now catches a stage exception at the stream boundary, logs `driver_error`, exits 5 and runs its bounded cleanup, where a malformed backend record or failed launch had let Phase 2 start and returned 0; `judge_c3` checks student values on all four teacher paths (it checked two); `c1_fp32_ref.py`'s `> 2×` median rule also applies at median 0. The new `test_driver_guards.py` failed on all five fault checks against the previous scripts and passes after the fix; `test_driver_cleanup.py` still passes 6/6 (receipts in `post-run/`). None of these fired in the recorded attempts. Notes: the [[decisions/start-multi-gpu-qualification-with-two-ranks|multi-GPU Decision]] cites the merged bundle instead of a pending-merge branch; the [[references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiled-GEMM Reference]] credits the depth-1 ATEN-only real-trunk backward above the bound and keeps the depth-8, production backend-claim wiring and guard-retirement gaps; the [[references/kaggriculture-teacher-distills-per-slot-kl-and-per-seat-winner-ce|teacher Reference]] scopes its CPU-only limit and records the C3/C4 GPU evidence, keeping cross-chunk/minibatch equality, multi-rank and trainer integration open. The [[references/index|References index]] lines follow. No GPU run. `just py-prepare`: 1,690 passed, 11 skipped, docs-fresh passes (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/merge-gpu-receipts-r1-fixes/py-prepare.log`); no Rust changed.
